		"LBL_HELP_AUTO": "Show help on screen",
		"LBL_HELP_INDEX_HINT": "Click one to see it again next to its control. The ones you have seen and the basics are listed here.",
		"LBL_HELP_INDEX_HINT_TOUCH": "Tap one to see it again next to its control. The ones you have seen and the basics are listed here.",
		"HELP_CAT_BASICS": "FIRST STEPS",
		"HELP_CAT_ECONOMY": "ECONOMY",
		"HELP_CAT_STORM": "STORM AND TAX",
		"HELP_CAT_ARMY": "ARMY AND COMBAT",
		"HELP_T_BUILD": "Building",
		"HELP_B_BUILD": "Opens the building list. Pick one and click on the map.",
		"HELP_B_BUILD_TOUCH": "Opens the building list. Pick one, tap the map and confirm with ✓.",
		"HELP_T_OBJECTIVE": "WHAT TO DO?",
		"HELP_B_OBJECTIVE": "In ☰ MENU: the next step. Do it and another appears.",
		"HELP_T_RESOURCES": "Resources and storage",
		"HELP_T_CAMERA": "Camera",
		"HELP_T_ZOOM": "Zoom and rotation",
		"HELP_T_MENUS": "☰ MENU",
		"HELP_B_MENUS": "Pauses the game and has it all: panels, save, settings and HELP.",
		"HELP_T_SKIRMISH": "Missions",
		"HELP_B_FIRST_STEPS": "The Core is your centre: it cannot be demolished and it never falls.\n\nFirst, always, a sawmill right next to a forest. Buildings that gather resources go right next to them: the gold mine beside a gold vein.\n\nThen a house. Almost every building needs people to run it: without workers it stands idle (Zzz).\n\nBUILD (bottom) opens the list. WASD or drag to move the camera, wheel to zoom, R to rotate before placing.",
		"HELP_B_FIRST_STEPS_TOUCH": "The Core is your centre: it cannot be demolished and it never falls.\n\nFirst, always, a sawmill right next to a forest. Buildings that gather resources go right next to them: the gold mine beside a gold vein.\n\nThen a house. Almost every building needs people to run it: without workers it stands idle (Zzz).\n\nBUILD (bottom) opens the list. Drag a finger to move the camera, pinch to zoom and use ↻ to rotate before placing.",
		"HELP_B_STORM": "The Storm does not come in the first minute: it comes when your smoke can be seen from the sea, with industry. And it does not hit all at once: the sky indicator tells you the phase.\n\nWARNING: ash on the horizon, nothing falls yet.\nASH: production drops and anything queued will be lost.\nSTORM: it breaks buildings.\nTAX: the Collectors come to collect.\n\nSpend beforehand what you do not want taken, repair afterwards what it breaks, and keep troops at home: win on the board and they take nothing.",
		"HELP_B_ARMY": "The path: sawmill, farm, gold mine, house, market, warehouse, foundry (era 2), barracks, home troops, refinery on a well (era 3), two towers, Headquarters. WHAT TO DO? always tells you the next step.\n\nHome troops: three infantry alone lose against the Collectors. Five units, two of them artillery, win. Standing towers reduce Storm damage and their gunners fight.\n\nOn the board a unit moves, then attacks. Artillery cannot fire at an adjacent enemy. Defending doubles defence until your next turn.\n\nHeadquarters at level 3 calls the Final Assault. Six tanks at home win it almost every time.",
		"HELP_TIP_TITHE_BODY": "They have come to collect the Tax. Your home troops fight on the board: win and they take nothing.\n\nLose, or have nothing to fight with, and they take a share of your storage. From the second visit on there is a minimum payment: if you cannot cover it, they take buildings and workers.",
		"HELP_TIP_BARRACKS_BODY": "Trains infantry (era 1), artillery (era 2) and tanks (era 3). Each barracks trains one unit at a time and you pay up front: open ARMY in the menu.\n\nAgainst the Collectors, three infantry alone always lose. Five units with two artillery win. From MISSIONS they go on expeditions for loot.",
		"HELP_TIP_CONSUMPTION_BODY": "Every villager eats 1 food per cycle. If it runs short, morale plunges and production with it; below 30 nobody is born.\n\nRight now: collect from your farms or buy food at the MARKET. Then more farms before more houses.",
		"HELP_TIP_AUDIT_BODY": "Headquarters at level 3 has called the Final Assault: 4 to 5 waves in a row against whatever is at home, with no training in between. Six tanks with four towers standing win it almost every time; with two towers, one time in two; three units, never.\n\nWhen you are ready, press LET THEM COME in MISSIONS. Losing does not end the game: it costs dearly and you can try again.",
		# ── linea-jugable ──
